@startuml seq-history
!include style.iuml
title Figure 7 (revised): Search, filter and sort the history — FR 5.4–5.6
actor User
participant ":HistoryFragment" as UI
participant ":HistoryViewModel" as VM
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR #D9F2DE
participant ":UserRepository" as UR #D9F2DE
participant ":TransactionRepository" as TR
participant ":HistoryFilter" as F
participant "db :\nFirebaseFirestore" as DB

User -> UI : open History tab (or return to it)
UI -> VM : load(groupId)
VM -[#2E7D32]> GR : NEW(getGroup(groupId, cb))
VM -[#2E7D32]> UR : NEW(getUsers(group.memberIds, cb))
note right of VM #D9F2DE : NEW: member names for the rows\nand for the member filter
VM -> TR : getTransactions(groupId, cb)
TR -> DB : get groups/{groupId}/transactions
TR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(transactions)
VM -> VM : all = transactions; query kept\n(HistoryQuery.defaults() the first time)
VM -> F : apply(all, query)
F --> VM : newest first
VM --> UI : visible (LiveData)
UI --> User : expenses and settlements; settlements labeled "Settlement";\nNEW(you lent / you borrowed on each row)
loop each change to keyword, type, category, member or sort order
  User -> UI : type a keyword, pick a filter chip, or toggle the sort
  UI -> VM : setKeyword(k) / setTypeFilter(t) / setCategoryFilter(c) /\nsetMemberFilter(uid) / setSortOrder(o), NEW(clearFilters())
  VM -> VM : update query; applyQuery()
  VM -> F : apply(all, query)
  F -> F : keep transactions matching the keyword and every filter;\nsort by createdAt (NEWEST_FIRST or OLDEST_FIRST)
  F --> VM : results
  VM --> UI : visible (LiveData), CHG(query copy for the chips)
  alt results are empty
    UI --> User : "Nothing matches" + Clear filters
  else results found
    UI --> User : matching transactions, NEW(Showing 3 of 12)
  end
end
note over VM, F : Filtering runs on the list already loaded;\nno database call is made
User -> UI : tap a transaction
UI --> User : open TransactionDetailActivity
@enduml
